cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "arduino-sim-rs: headless breadboard host and raylib GUI for the avr8rs AVR simulator"
abstract: >-
  The front-end for a native Rust AVR8 (ATmega328P-class) simulator: a headless
  breadboard host with simulated-time scheduling, external components and
  SPICE-deck electrical coupling, plus a raylib GUI that runs real Arduino
  sketches. The simulator engine itself is the `avr8rs` crate, developed in its
  own repository and consumed here from crates.io; the compatibility baseline it
  is validated against lives in `avr8js-parity`.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Navazhylau
    given-names: Michael
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/michaelnavazhylau/arduino-sim-rs"
url: "https://github.com/michaelnavazhylau/arduino-sim-rs"
keywords:
